   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "# Binc Stereo — video chain (windowed, image sequence out)\n\n`LoadVideo` → `GetVideoComponents.images` → **WINDOW** (`ImageFromBatch`) → **Depth Anything V2** → **Depth Temporal Filter** → **Stereo from Depth** → **eye L** / **eye R** PNG sequences in `output/binc-stereo/L/` and `/R/`.\n\n- A 4K take does not fit in RAM as one batch (≈24 GB per tensor). Run the WINDOW node at `batch_index` 0, 24, 48 … (same `length`) in order; `SaveImage` continues its numbering, so the folders fill up as one continuous sequence. Set `length` to the last window's remainder at the end.\n- Depth is normalised per window. For a locked convergence across windows, note `info`'s raw range on the first window and keep the same `lo/hi` percentiles; if convergence steps between windows, lower `hi_percentile` so it's less sensitive to outliers.\n- Core `SaveImage` writes 8-bit PNG. Assemble masters with e.g. `ffmpeg -framerate 24 -i eyeL_%05d_.png -c:v prores_ks -profile:v 3 -pix_fmt yuv422p10le eyeL.mov`.\n- Check `parallax_vis` first: near objects must read **dark**; if not, flip `depth_polarity`.\n- `report.summary.ok` false = a frame broke the parallax budget — adjust `convergence` or the budgets."
   ],
   "title": "READ FIRST"
  },
